3. Explain Pod Anti-Affinity
Interview Answer

"Pod Anti-Affinity is the opposite of Pod Affinity. It ensures that pods with certain labels are not scheduled on the same node or topology. It is mainly used to improve high availability."

Example

You have:

3 replicas

App-1
App-2
App-3

Without Anti-Affinity

Node1

App1
App2
App3

If Node1 crashes

All 3 pods gone ❌

With Pod Anti-Affinity

Node1
App1

Node2
App2

Node3
App3

Now if Node1 crashes

App1 ❌

App2 ✅

App3 ✅

Application is still available.
